{"name":"Zangief’s Chest","hex":"#823c3d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A box, now usually a large strong box with a secure convex lid.","A coffin."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit with one's chest (front of one's body)","To deposit in a chest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thorax","blocks":[{"text":"The thorax or chest is a part of the anatomy of mammals and other tetrapod animals located between the neck and the abdomen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Chest.jpg/330px-Chest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thorax"},{"title":"Zangief","blocks":[{"text":"Zangief is a fictional character in Capcom's Street Fighter series. The character was introduced as one of the eight playable characters in the video game Street Fighter II: The World Warrior (1991). In the game, Zangief primarily fights using grappling moves and is considered to be the first grappler-type fighting game character. The character was initially planned to be a strong but slow fighter placeholder named Vodka Golbalsky before eventually becoming a grappler after their name change, which derives from that of a Soviet wrestler. In the Street Fighter series, Zangief is a professional wrestler, nicknamed the Red Cyclone (赤きサイクロン), who hails from Russia and fights to prove the country's superiority by triumphing over other nations fighters in combat."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/70/Super_Zangief.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zangief"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Surface_projections_of_the_organs_of_the_trunk.png/500px-Surface_projections_of_the_organs_of_the_trunk.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u